new-lg4ff-dkms (0.5.0+git20261010.2092db1-1+stereo3d2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Install an edition udev rule (rules/70-sparky-*.rules) so the driver's
    sysfs controls are usable by the person at the wheel and no device node
    is made world-writable. Upstream fanatec.rules sets MODE="0666" on every
    0eb7 USB device; the edition rule uses uaccess instead and otherwise
    keeps the upstream file. hid-tmff2 and new-lg4ff ship no rules, their
    sysfs files were root-only; the edition rule gives them the group
    "games" convention of hid-fanatecff. Reasons in README.Debian.
  * Test: study/packages/rigs/check-wheel-udev.py fails on the previous build.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:30:00 -0300

